From 5fb68ef2b77613d61061cff3b9e865c46f7815b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:26:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a2xx: desktop GL fixes for Xenos found by piglit

- ir2: 1D and 3D texture lookups (the fetch constant carries the
  dimension), and shadow samplers compared in the shader (GL_LEQUAL only);
  ir2 used to abort on all three.
- ir2: a pixel shader that exports nothing (depth-only pass, no draw
  buffers) wedges Xenos; export a constant color.
- No color writes when the framebuffer has no color buffer.
- Don't sample k_32_32_32_FLOAT on Xenos: it is a vertex format only, and
  piglit draw-pixels hung the GPU through it.

piglit fbo-depth, draw-pixels, getteximage-formats, vertex-program-two-side,
glsl-fs-user-varying-ff and arb_clear_texture-depth no longer hang the GPU.

